(6443071, 956671, 10785, '<td valign="top">Technically good and accurate photo of the scene. Good focus, good color. All around good. How to get that extra pop to go from good to great?? Multiple exposures for the sky and foreground then merge and mask in post. Or use a graduated neutral density filter to darken the sunset sky. Use a polarizer which would only work well if the sun was to either side.</td>', 'Technically good and accurate photo of the scene. Good focus, good color. All around good. How to get that extra pop to go from good to great?? Multiple exposures for the sky and foreground then merge and mask in post. Or use a graduated neutral density filter to darken the sunset sky. Use a polarizer which would only work well if the sun was to either side.', '2011-06-13 14:27:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6443072, 956611, 96751, '<td valign="top">The lighting is sublime.  The tones, perfect.  Wonderful moment captured.</td>', 'The lighting is sublime.  The tones, perfect.  Wonderful moment captured.', '2011-06-13 14:27:55.000000', NULL, 1),
