(6448763, 956575, 83754, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mbrutus2009:</b></div><hr/><i> I would say the only thing here that is a bit distracting is the flash reflected in the eye. (I think this because the eye is right where my eye went). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the comment.  I also found the eyeflash a little distracting.  After comparing the original side by side with an edit where I took out the flash in the eye, it looked less natural and I went with the original - ultimtely because I liked it better.  Even in near darkness and no flash I''ve found it difficult to limit eye reflections in these birds.</td>', 'Originally posted by mbrutus2009: I would say the only thing here that is a bit distracting is the flash reflected in the eye. (I think this because the eye is right where my eye went).   Thank you for the comment.  I also found the eyeflash a little distracting.  After comparing the original side by side with an edit where I took out the flash in the eye, it looked less natural and I went with the original - ultimtely because I liked it better.  Even in near darkness and no flash I''ve found it difficult to limit eye reflections in these birds.', '2011-06-20 19:42:21.000000', NULL, 0),
