(6448860, 955988, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by olbol:</b></div><hr/><i> That must be some altitude to be so snowy in mid-June. What''s the nearest town to this area? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s in Grand Teton National Park, so the elevation is pretty high.  They have gotten more snow this year than any other year over the past 30 years.  Jackson, Wyoming is the closest town to it.  It was taken on June 7.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-20 21:24:59.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by olbol: That must be some altitude to be so snowy in mid-June. What''s the nearest town to this area?   It''s in Grand Teton National Park, so the elevation is pretty high.  They have gotten more snow this year than any other year over the past 30 years.  Jackson, Wyoming is the closest town to it.  It was taken on June 7.', '2011-06-20 22:24:25.000000', '2011-06-20 22:24:59.000000', 0),
